// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    The Paragon
// @category Cast / Character
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/The_Paragon
// @version  1.3
// @domain    Narrative
//
// Laconic: the moral exemplar — a character of incorruptible virtue who serves as the story's
// ethical standard, the one whose trustworthiness and loyalty are never in doubt. A cast archetype
// defined by TRAITS rather than role; its imply subsumes the virtue facts (Trustworthy, Loyal,
// Honourable) that a story spends on its most upright figures.

import "trl/concepts/index.trl"            // honor, integrity

assoc the_paragon -> [
  honor     : "the living standard of",
  integrity : "is the unbending"
]

// Archetype tags subsume the virtue facts real stories use on their upright characters.
imply Paragon -> [Virtuous, Trustworthy, Loyal, Honorable, Incorruptible, Narrative]

// Naming rule: incorruptible virtue SHOWN in a deed — standing up for the wronged when it costs —
// IS the Paragon. The virtue rides an EVENT ([&Protected], doing right at cost) so the rule is
// recalled; phase-2 coverage re-checks [+Virtuous] [+Incorruptible] on the bound doer — the
// positive constellation, present and acted, not merely asserted (STYLE §8).
rule The_Paragon {
  when:
    char $c [+Virtuous] [+Incorruptible]
    evt  $stand [&Protected(agent=$c, other=$wronged)]
  then:
    $c [+Paragon]
    $c -- honor
}

// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: The Ramayana — Rama protects the forest sages (Hindu, Valmiki) ===
// In exile in the Dandaka forest, Rama — Maryada Purushottama, the perfect man — finds the ascetics living
// in terror, preyed upon by the rakshasas who haunt the woods. Though it is not his own quarrel, and though
// it draws the demons' wrath down upon himself, he vows to rid the forest of them and stands as the sages'
// shield. He does right because it is right, at cost: the moral standard the epic is measured against.
char rama         [+Protagonist] [+Virtuous] [+Incorruptible]
char the_ascetics [+Innocent]   // the forest sages, preyed upon by the rakshasas

scene the_dandaka_forest {
  beat 1 {
    // Stands as shield for the persecuted sages though it is not his quarrel and draws the demons' wrath.
    evt the_vow [&Protected(agent=rama, other=the_ascetics)]
    // The_Paragon derives: rama [+Paragon] -- honor
  }
}
